It should all work in VC5 - that's what I've been using here. There's a
custom build command defined in the project so that .asm files assemble,
and there's a small .exe called 'Link.exe' which I wrote to translate
parameters that DevStudio is passing to the 32bit linker into ones the
old 16bit linker understands.

The upshot of all this is that you can build everything within the nice
cosy environment of VC5, use SourceSafe, get throwbacks etc.

There's just a couple of caveats - you should always do a 'rebuild all' -
(the incremental build doesn't always work), and release builds don't
work - these are both problems with my link wrapper that I'll fix as soon
as I get my copy of VC6 :-)

